          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Is asyncio?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Concurrency==: many tasks whose progress **overlaps** in time",
            "==Parallelism==: tasks run at the same instant on several cores",
            "asyncio gives you concurrency **only**, never parallelism",
            "Single-threaded ==cooperative multitasking==: one thread, many tasks",
            "A task keeps running until it **yields** at an `await`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How Switching Works",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def handle(conn):",
            "    req = await conn.read() # ⇄",
            "    n = count(req)   # no switch",
            "    await db.save(n)        # ⇄",
            "    await conn.write(n)     # ⇄"
          ],
          "note": "switches happen only at visible awaits"
        },
        {
