      "page_title": "The Event Loop",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What the Loop Is",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The ==event loop== is asyncio's **scheduler**",
            "{green:Ready queue}: callbacks that can run right now",
            "{blue:Timer heap}: callbacks due at a future time",
            "{purple:Watched fds}: sockets and pipes waiting for I/O"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "There is ==one running loop== per **thread**",
            "`asyncio.get_running_loop()` returns that loop",
            "If no loop is running, it raises `RuntimeError`"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. One Loop Iteration",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Run ready",
                "sub": "every callback",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "Timeout",
                "sub": "nearest timer",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Selector wait",
                "sub": "I/O or timeout",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "Queue ready",
                "sub": "new callbacks",
                "ink": "orange"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "OS",
            "Multiplexer",
            "Loop"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{icon:linux} Linux",
              "`epoll`",
              "Selector"
            ],
            [
              "macOS / BSD",
              "`kqueue`",
              "Selector"
            ],
            [
              "Windows",
              "==IOCP==",
              "Proactor (3.8+ default)"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Tasks are **driven** by callbacks",
            "Loop calls ==Task.__step()== from the ready queue",
            "Each step advances the coroutine by one `send()`"
          ],
          "style": "number"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Scheduling APIs",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()",
            "loop.call_soon(print, \"now\")",
            "loop.call_later(2, print, \"+2s\")",
            "t = loop.time() + 5",
            "loop.call_at(t, print, \"at t\")"
          ],
          "note": "call_at uses loop.time(), not wall clock"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "API",
            "Runs cb",
            "Caller"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`call_soon(cb)`",
              "next iteration",
              "loop thread"
            ],
            [
              "`call_later(d, cb)`",
              "after d sec",
              "loop thread"
            ],
            [
              "`call_at(when, cb)`",
              "at loop time",
              "loop thread"
            ],
            [
              "`call_soon_threadsafe`",
              "next iteration",
              "**any** thread"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Thread safety",
          "items": [
            "The loop is **NOT** thread-safe",
            "From another thread, use only:",
            "`loop.call_soon_threadsafe(cb)`",
            "`asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe(coro, loop)`"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Debug & Speed",
