    {
      "page_title": "asyncio.run: The Entry Point",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is asyncio.run?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.run(main())` = the standard ==sync-to-async bridge==",
            "Plain sync code calls it and gets `main()`'s result back",
            "Normally called **once** per program, at the top level",
            "Covered on p.3: the loop it creates and drives"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. What run() does",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Creates a **new** event loop and sets it current for this thread",
            "Runs `main()` to completion: returns its result or re-raises its exception",
            "Cleanup: cancels leftovers, shuts down async gens and the executor, closes the loop"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Cleanup call",
            "Purpose"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "cancel leftover tasks",
              "stop stragglers"
            ],
            [
              "`loop.shutdown_asyncgens()`",
              "finalize async gens"
            ],
            [
              "`shutdown_default_executor()`",
              "join thread pool (3.9+)"
            ],
            [
              "`loop.close()`",
              "release the loop"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example pattern",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "import asyncio",
            "",
            "async def main():",
            "    return await work()",
            "",
            "if __name__ == '__main__':",
            "    asyncio.run(main())  # once"
          ],
          "note": "one call, at the script's top"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Runner (Python 3.11+)",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "with asyncio.Runner() as runner:",
            "    runner.run(setup())",
            "    runner.run(main())  # same loop"
          ],
          "note": "one loop reused across run() calls"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Already inside a loop?",
          "items": [
            "Jupyter, or inside another coroutine → loop already running",
            "`asyncio.run()` there raises **RuntimeError**",
            "Fix: write `await main()` instead"
          ],
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Fire-and-forget tasks get ==cancelled silently== when `main` returns",
            "`asyncio.run` per request or inside a `for`: new loop each time",
            "That's **slow** and breaks resources bound to a loop",
            "Lock, Queue, client sessions made on loop A **fail** on loop B",
            "`asyncio.run` inside a running loop → RuntimeError"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Wrong",
            "Right"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "run() per request",
              "one run(), long-lived loop"
            ],
            [
              "run() in Jupyter",
              "`await main()`"
            ],
            [
              "many run() calls",
              "`asyncio.Runner()` (3.11+)"
            ],
            [
              "un-awaited background task",
              "await it before return"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Shutdown gotcha",
